WEBVTT

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.730
No! Don't!

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:37.480
That teddy bear was my birthday present!

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.040
It's a really special bear that Mama and Papa gave me...

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.000
That's wrong.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:47.490
I'm your papa, aren't I?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.200
Listen, if you misbehave...

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:00.530
your precious treasures will be burned.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:01.880
And...

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.850
you'll be burned too.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.690
The kidnapper demanding a ransom

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:27.230
is most likely after the Beliz inheritance.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.250
No, I think—

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.650
Pardon me.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.810
Oh, there it is.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.210
Zenigata.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.970
Not only did he fail to apprehend Mine Fujiko,

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.930
he lost his subordinate and can't pursue Lupin.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.430
He's finished.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.730
I'm hungry.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.920
Let's go get something to eat.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:56.190
I'll devour it all.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.850
Are you alone?

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:05.360
Yes.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.730
No, she's not.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.490
She's with me.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.100
Why did he imitate you?

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.250
Who knows?

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.390
Don't feign innocence.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.480
We couldn't find Oscar's body.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.640
You got rid of it, didn't you,

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.320
Mine Fujiko?

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.900
Is that <i>really </i>what you think happened?

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:33.760
Hey.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.940
If you're planning to get revenge for that boy,

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.610
team up with me.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:45.250
Sending you to the electric chair will be my revenge for him.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.020
Really now?

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.970
The kidnapping cases involving girls has been a hot topic lately...

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:54.730
Rather, the <i>serial</i> kidnapping case.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.100
Serial? What are you talking about?

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:01.290
Well, it's true that lately kidnappings have been happening all over the world,

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.150
but there's no connection between the locations and situations.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.270
You can't call it "serial" when the culprits are all different.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.790
There's a commonality.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:14.080
An artwork or a painting has been left in the room of each victim.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.810
The subjects varied, but it always involved an owl.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.450
Owl?

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:20.310
Don't tell me...

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.520
Luis Yu Almeida.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.390
Bingo.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:27.440
You don't disappoint.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:38.000
I'll be your partner for a while. Let's try to get along.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.890
You're just planning on using
my corpse as a stepping stone.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.590
That's the kind of woman you are.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.090
Count me out.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.400
Don't be such a downer.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:57.310
If I'm talking about a treasure possessed by the world-leading manufacturers Glaucus Pharmaceuticals,

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.120
then you know it has to be something special.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.610
There's only one thing I want.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.650
You can have everything else.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.500
Is it Mine Fujiko?

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.380
Why are you obsessed with that crazy woman?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.740
I don't get it.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.350
Do you need to get your eyes checked?

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.210
She's a treasure of the highest quality.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.690
Yep, she's a puppet

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.880
of intricate craftsmanship!

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.900
This is the place, right?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.850
Yes.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.570
Glaucus Park.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.400
May I see your ticket?

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.030
Ticket?

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.750
Ticket...

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.160
I wouldn't have one in here...

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:00.410
This is...

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.050
Talk about bad taste.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:14.800
What?

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.860
House of...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.560
Fujiko.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.960
What is this?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.720
This is...

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.050
the deserted town, Eulenspiegel.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.190
The place where I was raised...

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.390
is the town of Glaucus Pharmaceuticals.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.270
Right...

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:18.290
My papa was conducting an experiment in the lab.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:22.120
He said that it was an experiment that would make everyone happy.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.260
And...

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.760
Hey!

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.160
Where are we?

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:46.250
No way.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:51.690
Papa took me to a place with many other girls...

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.520
Mine Fujiko.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.280
Suddenly, Papa...

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.140
just disappeared...

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:16.170
and I...

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:26.200
...went to the castle in the sky.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.600
<i>Fujiko.</i>

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.880
Did you hear... a voice?

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.330
What's wrong, Mine Fujiko?

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.580
This is your story,

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.140
Fujiko.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.670
I was so lonely.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.630
I've been longing to see you.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.470
Mine Fujiko.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.920
The lab?

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.180
Yes.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.140
I was summoned to the castle in the sky.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:07.890
And there...

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.140
I was experimented on.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.640
Stop...

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.620
Stop it!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.950
No more!

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.210
Hey, get a grip!

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.500
Let go of me!

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.390
This way!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.720
Your ticket?

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:48.510
Let's see.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:49.350
Over here?

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:53.820
I thought so.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.310
When did that...

00:09:56.380 --> 00:10:00.070
Lupin III, this is definitely a trap.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.000
If we're to turn back, now is the time.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.240
Oh, ice cream!

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.560
That was a waste.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.060
The Fräulein Eule cult

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:31.100
was a front for the experimental facility run by Glaucus Pharmaceutical, which was controlled by Count Almeida.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:39.130
Count Almeida hired me to steal Mine Fujiko, who had infiltrated the cult.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:43.610
She's a woman that the Count is strangely attached to.

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.610
She piqued my interest.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.370
And when I looked her up,

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.320
I discovered that a woman named Mine Fujiko

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:52.750
never existed in this world.

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:55.990
She's a thief.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:58.630
Of course she would use a false name.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:02.940
I'm saying that there was no one who could possibly be her.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.250
Meaning?

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.000
Meaning that the famous female thief Mine Fujiko...

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:14.210
had her whole life, the story named "Mine Fujiko", stolen away.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.650
You saw it, right?

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:22.910
Fujiko tried to kill a woman whose life was controlled by others.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:29.000
She probably saw a reflection of herself

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.720
in the powerless woman who was at the whim of others.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.230
By killing that woman,

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.540
she believed she could kill her past self.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.680
In any case, it has nothing to do with me.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:47.100
It's too late for that, unfortunately.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.400
In the story of "Mine Fujiko"

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:56.530
we've already become recurring characters.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:57.680
What?

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:00.360
See? We've got a welcoming party.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:16.970
I appreciate the invitation.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.130
You're the one who gave us tickets, right?

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:24.940
I have a request to make of you today.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.720
I will steal Mine Fujiko.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.300
But after that I'm doing what I want with her.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:33.700
Today's request is different.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:34.560
What is it?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.630
Lupin III,

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.810
I want you to kill Mine Fujiko.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:41.220
Huh?

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:44.070
If you refuse this request...

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:48.520
Wait!

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:13.760
Wow, what a thrill!

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.490
Tell me, Lupin.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.070
Why do I have to get involved in this?

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:30.910
Count Almeida has kept tabs on Mine Fujiko's every move!

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:34.240
He's the reason for many of the things she's been through!

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.880
That includes her meeting with us!

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.140
Uh oh!

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.200
It may not end with just us!

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:01.600
There's probably an entire idiotic cast of characters who got caught up in this tale!

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:06.630
Where am I?

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:11.490
If I recall correctly, I was cornered
by men wearing owl masks,

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.330
and then I...

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.210
Shall I meet my end here...

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.550
without determining the true nature of Mine Fujiko?

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:43.120
Wait, I don't understand.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:45.110
What is Almeida after?

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.150
What's he after?

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.400
Well, let's find out.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.070
Hey!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.400
Will this gun make you talk?

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.060
My goal...

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.380
is love.

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:15.830
Dammit!

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:16.930
Where the hell is the exit?

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.610
More! More!

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.600
There's no point in shooting dolls!

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.450
Then...!

00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:46.540
Then let's get out of here!

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:51.460
Get me... out of here.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.090
Mine Fujiko.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.090
I...

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.600
wanted to escape.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.240
From my wounded,

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.610
cursed existence.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:20.370
If I covered myself in finery,

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.560
the wounds inflicted on me were hidden.

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:25.900
I finally sealed them away.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:28.930
I sealed them away in a treasure chest.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:30.860
Yes.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.190
With your strong will,

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:38.940
you sealed away your memories of the past.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:41.180
Those days of love with me.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.910
That is why, in order to open your heart,

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.740
I have prepared many keys.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:55.400
I will mix your story with mine once again.

00:16:55.400 --> 00:17:00.410
They have already fulfilled their role as keys.

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:06.410
Now that Mine Fujiko's memories have returned, we have no more use for you.

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:10.420
Then, why did you tell me about Mine Fujiko's past?

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:13.970
The illusion I saw in that deserted town...

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:16.830
You showed that to me, didn't you?

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.920
Deserted town?

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.430
Yeah.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:23.890
The professor with the shiny, bald head told me.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:26.430
"Save my daughter," he said.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:32.340
I see.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.850
He did something like that?

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:43.820
If you refuse to kill her, then I have no choice. I will do it myself—

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.620
Damn! Wait!

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:58.300
<i>This is not only Mine Fujiko's story.</i>

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:02.340
<i>It is </i>our<i> story.</i>

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:07.350
Not just Mine Fujiko's?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.520
<i>Our</i> story, huh?

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.660
Mine Fujiko!

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:20.560
Your death day will be in three months, on the 15th!

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:22.930
What day is it?!

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:25.080
Huh? It's the 15th.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.780
Mine Fujiko's death day.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:29.370
Death day?

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.110
Mine Fujiko.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.620
Move!

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:46.140
Stop it!

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.140
These aren't dolls!

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:55.650
Look closely!

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:58.190
They all look similar to you!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.570
They're all failed prototypes!

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:19.880
This is...

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.220
Hey, stop it!

00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:30.600
Go!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.350
Mine Fujiko!

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:35.600
Leave this one to me.

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.740
Who did that?

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.360
Was it Mine Fujiko?

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:55.370
Let's go, Jigen Daisuke.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.370
It's you, isn't it?

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.350
Oscar.

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:32.410
<i>I remember everything.</i>

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.160
<i>If I climb these steps</i>

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:40.170
<i>and open that door...</i>

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.440
<i>there will be...</i>

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:50.850
I've been longing to see you,

00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:51.680
Fujiko.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:55.430
Fujiko,

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.940
come sit on my lap.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.860
Sit on my lap.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:11.370
If you disobey me, I'll punish you again.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:16.030
I'll burn you.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:20.050
Forgive me!

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:25.580
Papa!
